#: ../../technical/articles/192-aeat-official-reference-corpus.md:10
msgid "Scope and sampling method"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/192-aeat-official-reference-corpus.md:12
msgid ""
"This chunk inventories 876 files totaling 290,532,686 bytes (about 290.5 "
"MB) under `corpus/aeat_official`. The inventory metadata was parsed for "
"every file; I did not load the full PDF, Excel, or extracted-text "
"collection into context. I sampled across the record-design archive, "
"current calendar and procedure pages, official blank forms, "
"SII/VERI*FACTU schemas, identity references, GROI response fixtures, "
"retired-model notice, tax-law update notice, and Renta Web Open page. "
"Within the workbook subset I sampled a current Modelo 303 layout and a "
"large Modelo 200 layout, including bounded parts of their generated "
"sidecars. The complete source-link appendix is generated from the chunk "
"manifest; it is inventory coverage, not a claim that all 876 contents "
"received semantic review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/192-aeat-official-reference-corpus.md:14
msgid "Corpus capabilities and sampled behavior"
msgstr "Capacitats del corpus i comportament mostrejat"

#: ../../technical/articles/192-aeat-official-reference-corpus.md:16
msgid ""
"The largest section is `disenos_registro`: 731 files and about 271.8 MB. "
"Its top-level catalog identifies 58 model directories and 254 source "
"artifacts, while the larger on-disk count includes original "
"workbooks/PDFs, extracted JSON/Markdown sidecars, correction metadata, "
"and per-model manifests. The catalog records source pages, retrieval "
"dates, file names, sizes, and SHA-256 values. It spans current and "
"historical model layouts. For example, the archived 2026-and-later Modelo"
" 303 record design defines a fixed-width exchange with record/page "
"discriminators, field positions and lengths, field types, validations, "
"and permitted period shapes; it also marks its use from exercise 2026. "
"Its generated extraction is divided into seven sections. The sidecar "
"reports `status: ok`, and its source hash matches the archived workbook. "
"The 2025 Modelo 200 archive similarly includes a 11.5 MB XLS workbook and"
" an extraction with 77 sections whose source hash matches; older annual "
"models are retained as PDF revisions. These formats can support reading "
"and producing official filing exchange layouts, but this chunk does not "
"establish which parser/exporter consumes them or whether the extracted "
"fields agree with every source page. See the record-design catalog "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/disenos_registro/manifest.json`),"
" Modelo 303 manifest "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/disenos_registro/modelo_303/manifest.json`),"
" archived 2026 Modelo 303 workbook "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/disenos_registro/modelo_303/files/01-303-ejercicio-2026-y"
"-siguientes-actualizado-28-01-26-378-kb-xlsx.xlsx`), its extracted "
"record-layout text "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/disenos_registro/modelo_303/files/01-303-ejercicio-2026-y"
"-siguientes-actualizado-28-01-26-378-kb-xlsx.xlsx.extracted.md`), and the"
" 2025 Modelo 200 package "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/disenos_registro/modelo_200/manifest.json`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/192-aeat-official-reference-corpus.md:18
msgid ""
"The 112 files in `instructions` (about 7.4 MB) and nine calendar files "
"(about 10.2 MB) supply operational references. A sampled AEAT 2026 "
"domiciliation page distinguishes monthly from quarterly models and gives "
"separate bank-debit and filing windows; its table includes monthly and "
"quarterly Modelo 303/353 cases, illustrating why cadence and payment "
"method must be read from the dated calendar rather than assumed. The "
"Modelo 303 procedure page is an AEAT workflow/links page rather than a "
"machine schema. The archive also has 121 PDFs and many captured HTML "
"sources and extracted derivatives. Retrieval and publication dates make "
"the material traceable, but the repository snapshot is not a live "
"deadline service. See the 2026 domiciliation calendar "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/calendars/files/calendario-"
"contribuyente-2026-domiciliacion.html`) and Modelo 303 procedure page "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/instructions/modelo_303/files/modelo-303-procedure.html`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/192-aeat-official-reference-corpus.md:20
msgid ""
"Ten published-form files include blank Modelo 145 and 840 PDFs with "
"extracted text and provenance manifests. The sampled Modelo 145 form "
"communicates a recipient's personal/family circumstances to a payer for "
"withholding; the 840 form covers IAE registration/change/withdrawal. They"
" are document templates and field guidance, not evidence about any "
"taxpayer. A separate `renta_web_open` page expressly describes Renta Web "
"Open as a simulator that does not validate the NIF and cannot submit a "
"return. That distinction helps prevent a simulation from being "
"represented as filing. See the Modelo 145 extraction "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/formularios_publicados/modelo_145/files/mod145_es_es.pdf.extracted.md`),"
" Modelo 840 extraction "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/formularios_publicados/modelo_840/files/01-840"
"-modelo-declaracion-iae-alta-variacion-baja-pdf.pdf.extracted.md`), and "
"Renta Web Open page "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/renta_web_open/renta-web-"
"open.html`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/192-aeat-official-reference-corpus.md:22
msgid ""
"The five-file `einvoice_record_schemas` directory is more precisely a set"
" of SII and VERI*FACTU AEAT record-supply web-service schemas, not "
"document-level e-invoice formats; the manifest points to the separate "
"Facturae corpus for that. The manifest says the exact family directory "
"and original filenames are load-bearing because both families import "
"`SuministroInformacion.xsd` by relative name. Static XML parsing "
"confirmed that each family has its own same-named base schema and target "
"namespace, and that each `SuministroLR.xsd` imports its local base. SII's"
" envelope declares 17 top-level record elements; the sampled VERI*FACTU "
"envelope declares one. The manifest dates this single snapshot to "
"2026-08-07 and notes that the schemas expose no version attribute, so the"
" bundle cannot independently identify a later protocol revision. I "
"checked XML well-formedness and the import structure only; no XML Schema "
"engine or remote imports were executed. The manifest says VERI*FACTU is "
"included for a refusal path rather than a product capability, which is a "
"stated scope rationale rather than independently verified consumer "
"behavior. See the schema manifest "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/einvoice_record_schemas/manifest.json`),"
" SII envelope "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/einvoice_record_schemas/sii/SuministroLR.xsd`),"
" and VERI*FACTU envelope "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/einvoice_record_schemas/verifactu/SuministroLR.xsd`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/192-aeat-official-reference-corpus.md:24
msgid ""
"The sampled 2022 Modelo 220 `.xlsm` has an external-workbook relationship"
" targeting `DR220e22_5.xlsm`; that target is not among the archived "
"Modelo 220 files. The ZIP package did not contain a `vbaProject.bin`, so "
"this sample did not show an embedded VBA project, but spreadsheet "
"software could still offer or attempt to refresh the external link. Any "
"preview/import workflow should suppress automatic link updates and keep "
"parsing isolated. This observation is limited to one workbook and is not "
"evidence that a product path opens it. See the archived 2022 Modelo 220 "
"workbook "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/disenos_registro/modelo_220/files/02-220-ejercicio-2022.xlsm`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/192-aeat-official-reference-corpus.md:26
msgid ""
"The three identity pages provide NIF/NIE composition and check-digit "
"guidance. Two are AEAT pages; the third is a DGOJ page stored under the "
"AEAT corpus directory. That DGOJ HTML contains inline JavaScript and a "
"remote Matomo tracker URL. Nothing here proves that the product renders "
"the page, but any path that opens it as active HTML should treat it as "
"executable remote-origin content rather than passive text. The 3-file "
"GROI sample set is more explicit about provenance: its audit note says "
"the small response fragments were captured from the authenticated AEAT "
"service on 2026-05-07 and that raw capture artifacts are not committed. "
"The sample set includes a positive operator response and an invalid-NIF "
"refusal, which can help anchor parser behavior but does not cover the "
"service's complete response vocabulary. See the identity references "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/identity/aeat-nif-personas-"
"fisicas.html`), DGOJ reference "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/identity/dgoj-nif-nie-"
"control.html`), and GROI provenance "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/groi_response_samples/PROVENANCE.md`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/192-aeat-official-reference-corpus.md:28
msgid ""
"The corpus also contains one retired-Modelo-037 notice, one April 2026 "
"AEAT note about the tax effects of two Royal Decree-Laws, and other "
"official forms and service pages. These are time-sensitive references. "
"The retired-model notice is stored as a 24,141-byte single-line `.txt` "
"file that fails strict UTF-8 decoding (a replacement decoder reports 134 "
"replacement characters); its initial text contains a BOE page and HTML "
"entities. A consumer must not assume this particular file is clean, line-"
"oriented UTF-8 without checking its actual decoding path. See the "
"retirement notice "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/historical_retired_modelos/modelo_037/files/BOE-A-2025-410"
"-orden-hac-1526-2024-supresion-m037.txt`) and 2026 tax-effects note "
"(`src/cadrumo/_data/corpus/aeat_official/notices/aeat-nota-efectos-"
"rdl-16-2025-rdl-2-2026.html`)."
msgstr ""

